  "title": "Syabrubesi to Rasuwagadhi (Pelican) — Post-event Imagery",
  "description": "Very-high-resolution Pelican coverage of the flood corridor, acquired 06:10 UTC on 27 August 2026, about four hours after the SkySat collects and roughly a day after the flood. Three sequential frames run north from Syabrubesi to the Rasuwagadhi border crossing, overlapping the SkySat footprints. At roughly 0.55 m ground sample distance this is the sharpest imagery in the catalog. Planet reports 83–85% cloud and a clear fraction of 0% for all three frames, but that clear figure is not consistent with the imagery: each frame carries substantial interpretable ground, including a bright sediment-laden river channel traceable along the corridor. Treat the reported clear fraction with caution and inspect the scenes directly. 3 scenes; each Item carries the available visual, pansharpened, udm2 assets.",
